<p>Hungary&#x27;s outgoing prime minister, Viktor Orban, said on April 25 that he will not take up the parliamentary seat he won on the Fidesz-KDNP list after his party&#x27;s heavy defeat in the April 12 election, ending an uninterrupted 36-year run in the legislature. Orban said he is needed not in parliament but in reorganizing the political camp he leads, while also signaling that he wants to remain head of Fidesz if party members renew their confidence in him at a congress planned for June. The move follows a decisive election victory by Peter Magyar&#x27;s Tisza party, which won 141 of the 199 seats in Hungary&#x27;s National Assembly, while Fidesz fell to 52 after 16 years in power. The result opens the way for a major political transition in Hungary, with Tisza&#x27;s supermajority potentially helping pass democratic reforms tied to the possible release of about €17 billion in European Union funds frozen over rule-of-law concerns during Orban&#x27;s tenure.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/vn-fqpn17bqECeu256lLMD8YzjitnBIt0kdD7S-ZZkKOIV94iyTJxXaVKTYarya5KD_Xt_l6N4yhWYKUjlZcgpLCP2NayroCN9duCN784VvtzrwgtVU42Ctc0F0nRlSVzaAvMtAHgaYD6f7M_i90UJ-HwMBxyZyUl_nrEiWBoFeGkF0_1ACFHDX5hAc32t_5_gBgyVtH5rbyKPeZkibhEjLdjioyofWdHw92v_yi5Absp49MCMow4fzncYvAfzNZYg4DZTmJKOkHa1laTg' alt='Outgoing Hungarian Prime Minister Viktor Orban delivers a press statement in front of the Presidential Sandor Palace in Budapest on April 15, 2026, three days after general elections in Hungary.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Faction overhaul: Orban said Fidesz&#x27;s parliamentary group would be &quot;radically transformed,&quot; with Gergely Gulyas set to lead the new caucus when it forms on Monday.</li><li>Magyar&#x27;s response: Peter Magyar wrote on social media that Orban &quot;is still incapable of one thing: taking responsibility&quot; after the former prime minister announced he would give up his seat.</li><li>Long dominance: Orban has been one of the defining figures in Hungarian politics since the fall of communism in 1989 and has led Fidesz throughout the post-1990 parliamentary era.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Viktor Orban: He framed surrendering his mandate as returning a seat that belongs to the Fidesz list and said his focus should shift to rebuilding the broader nationalist-patriotic movement rather than serving in the chamber. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639074-orban-steps-down-hungarian-parliament/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Peter Magyar: The Tisza leader responded to Orban&#x27;s announcement by arguing that the former prime minister was still avoiding personal accountability despite the scale of the election defeat. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/orban-relinquishes-seat-in-hungarys-parliament/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Fidesz leadership: Party leaders proposed that Orban stay on as Fidesz president and oversee a restructuring process, suggesting they still want him to shape the party&#x27;s recovery despite the loss. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/orban-relinquishes-seat-in-hungarys-parliament/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>International media analysis: Several outlets described the resignation from parliament as a sign that Orban is stepping back institutionally while trying to preserve influence through party leadership and internal renewal. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cd9v1wll8qqo'>BBC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/25/hungary-s-orban-will-not-sit-in-parliament-after-election-defeat_6752826_4.html'>Hungary&#x27;s Orban will not sit in parliament after election defeat</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cd9v1wll8qqo'>Orbán steps down from Hungarian parliament after landslide defeat</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3351444/hungarys-orban-wont-take-parliament-seat-after-landslide-loss-wants-lead-renewal'>Hungary’s Orban won’t take up parliament seat after landslide loss, wants to lead renewal</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/hungarys-orban-will-not-sit-in-parliament-after-election-loss'>Hungary’s Orban will not sit in Parliament after election loss</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/viktor-orban-steps-back-from-parliament-after-landslide-loss-vows-to-rebuild-hungarys-national-side/article70906558.ece'>Viktor Orbán steps back from Parliament after landslide loss, vows to rebuild Hungary’s ’national side’</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/25/world/europe/viktor-orban-fidesz.html'>Crushed at the Polls, Hungary’s Former Ruling Party Licks Its Wounds</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/orbn-steps-back-after-landslide-loss-vowing-rebuild-132382122'>Orbán steps back after a landslide loss, vowing to rebuild Hungary’s &#x27;national side&#x27;</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639074-orban-steps-down-hungarian-parliament/'>Orban steps down from Hungarian parliament</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/orban-relinquishes-seat-in-hungarys-parliament/'>Orbán relinquishes seat in Hungary’s parliament</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-orban-will-not-take-seat-in-hungarys-parliament-after-landslide/'>Orbán will not take seat in Hungary’s parliament after landslide election loss</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li></ul>